        <mxCell id="e_glapi" value="GitLab REST API · 443" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#C2185B;labelBackgroundColor=#F5F5F5;fontSize=11;exitX=0.25;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="glmcp" target="gitlab">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="1490" y="1330" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="note1" value="&lt;b&gt;Why the invoke path is drawn outside the VPC&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;start_review.py does &lt;b&gt;not&lt;/b&gt; reach into a private subnet. A CI runner has no network path into the VPC — no PrivateLink, VPN or Direct Connect is deployed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The invoke path is a &lt;b&gt;public regional API&lt;/b&gt; (bedrock-agentcore.&lt;i&gt;region&lt;/i&gt;.amazonaws.com), authenticated with SigV4/IAM. Your VPC is attached to the runtimes for &lt;b&gt;egress only&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;S3 is therefore not inside the VPC either — only the S3 Files &lt;i&gt;mount targets&lt;/i&gt; live there (page 2)." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=1;fillColor=#FFF8E1;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontSize=11;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1000" width="320" height="340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b&gt;Legend&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=&quot;#8C4FFF&quot;&gt;━━&lt;/font&gt; invoke plane (public regional API, SigV4)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=&quot;#01A88D&quot;&gt;━━&lt;/font&gt; A2A agent-to-agent&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=&quot;#E7157B&quot;&gt;╍╍&lt;/font&gt; MCP tool call via Gateway&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=&quot;#7AA116&quot;&gt;━━&lt;/font&gt; storage (NFS / objects)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=&quot;#DD344C&quot;&gt;╍╍&lt;/font&gt; identity / secrets&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=&quot;#C2185B&quot;&gt;━━&lt;/font&gt; external SaaS&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=&quot;#879196&quot;&gt;╍╍&lt;/font&gt; observability&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Key principle:&lt;/b&gt; agents never mount S3 Files — only the two MCP servers carry the NFS mount. Agents reach storage exclusively through Gateway-governed MCP tools.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Per-run isolation:&lt;/b&gt; workspaces/{repo}/{mr}/{correlation_id}/ — enables concurrent reviews, audit trail and re-runs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Icon note:&lt;/b&gt; AgentCore runtimes, Gateway and the data-plane API share the mxgraph.aws4.bedrock_agentcore stencil; they are distinguished by label, not by icon." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B1B7BE;fontSize=11;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="440" y="1400" width="1780" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

